# SYNTHESISED to exercise the swimlane timeline's lane-scrolling window: five
# RPC spans that all cover the exact same interval, so PackLanes' greedy
# packing (a span goes into the first lane whose last span has already
# finished) cannot reuse any earlier lane for a later span and opens a new
# one each time -- five fully-overlapping spans force five lanes,
# deterministically, rather than leaving the count to depend on a packing
# heuristic this fixture would then have to explain. The line shape is
# testdata/two-providers.log's "Received downstream response" verbatim. The
# first line is not itself a response: it exists only to anchor the
# scanner's base clock a few seconds before the first real span, so that
# span's start is not clamped to zero by ReportedBuilder (see the doc
# comment on span.Span). Values are invented; no line here is from a real
# run.
